Release number 18 / Serial number 850919

"Jeff, snap out of it!" cries Tip Randall, bursting into your laboratory. "The alert signal is on!"
You look up from your plans for the SCIMITAR, a top-secret submarine that's still being tested. It's designed for capturing marine life on the ocean floor. You notice the alarm bell on the videophone ringing. Someone's trying to reach you over the private videophone network of Inventions Unlimited!


Okay, Jeff, what do you want to do now?
>turn on videophone
As the alarm bell stops ringing, a picture of a woman holding a microphone appears, and you can hear her voice from the speaker. But both sound and picture are fuzzy.
(Your score just went up by 1 point!)

What next?
>get microphone
(Your score just went up by 1 point!)
You are now holding the microphone.

What next?
>turn on microphone
Okay, the microphone is now on.

What next?
>tune videophone
Ah, that's better! You recognize the woman as Commander Bly, who's in charge of the Undersea Research Station of Inventions Unlimited, called the Aquadome, just off the Atlantic coast. "Jeff! Jeff!" she's saying. "This is the Aquadome calling the Nyman Research Lab! We have an urgent problem!"
(Your score just went up by 1 point!)

What next?
>ask bly about problem
"Jeff! Jeff! Our transparent dome enclosing the Undersea Research Station is being battered by a huge monster!"

What next?
>bye
"I hope to see you soon, Jeff."

Something's wrong! The picture vanished from your videophone screen, and the sound conked out!
Tip says, "That's strange! Maybe you should use the Computestor."
(Oh no! Your score just went down by 3 points!)

What next?
>drop microphone
Okay, the microphone is now on the floor.

What next?
>e. e
(east part)
You're in the east part of your laboratory. A doorway leads out through a corridor to the office of your lab assistant, Sharon Kemp. A Microwave Security Scanner stands against the wall. An intercom sits on the lab desk.

(corridor)
You're in a corridor, with your laboratory to the west, a storage closet to the south, and Kemp's office to the east. An Electrical Panel fills most of the north wall.

Tip follows you into the corridor.
(If you want a clue, find Infocard #3 in your SEASTALKER package. Read hidden clue #1 and put "Electrical Panel" in the blank space.)

What next?
>look at panel
A circuit breaker on the Electrical Panel is open. This circuit breaker controls the power to the videophone and other equipment in the private videophone network.
Tip says, "How did that happen? You didn't overload the circuit."

(Are you tired of seeing "What next?" Well, you won't see it any more.)

>close breaker
Okay, the circuit breaker is now closed.
(Your score just went up by 3 points!)

>w. s. s. w
(east part)

Tip follows you into the east part.
As you re-enter the lab, Tip says, "Look, Jeff! The videophone's working again! There's a normal test pattern on the screen!"

(If you want a clue, find Infocard #8 in your SEASTALKER package. Read hidden clue #1 and put "SCIMITAR" in the blank space.)

(south part)
You're in the south part of your laboratory, next to shelves full of chemical and electronic supplies. A door leads south to the test tank.

(north walkway)
You're at a temporary runway or gangplank that leads from the walkway to the entry hatch of the SCIMITAR. The entry hatch is open.
The test tank (which is now empty of sea water) is located in a large work room, just south of your laboratory, with concrete-block walls on three sides and a high metal roof. Most of its floor is dug out and lined with steel, to form the huge tank used for developing and testing underwater gear and the pilot models of your submarine craft.
There's a walkway around the tank on three sides -- north, west and south. On the east side, a steel gate forms the wall of the room.

Tip follows you into the north walkway.

(west walkway)
Tip is off to the north.
Sitting on the work counter is:
  a catalyst capsule

>get capsule
(Your score just went up by 5 points!)
You are now holding the catalyst capsule.

>n. s
(north walkway)
Tip is here.

(SCIMITAR)
You're in the pilot's seat of the SCIMITAR, its operating control panel before you.
A wraparound viewport, both fore and aft, provides a view ahead and astern. You can also observe your surroundings with a sonarscope and a hydrophone listening device. There's a sonarphone for communication. You'll discover other features when you need them.
Tip is sitting behind you, reading a magazine.
The power reactor is off and open.
(Your score just went up by 1 point!)

>ask tip for magazine
Tip hands you the magazine.

>open magazine
You open the magazine and see an article.

>read article
It says that Doctor Jerome Thorpe may have created synthetic forms of marine life by genetic engineering. You learn that Thorpe went into hiding to duck publicity, but before that he told friends he would soon marry Sharon Kemp.
The form of the creatures is unknown. They may be stimulated by ultrasonic pulses and might be trained to respond to such pulses.
Some scientists are skeptical, but Thorpe has claimed that one-celled organisms had evolved in his lab from AMINO-HYDROPHASE or A.H. If rumors are true, these synthetic sea creatures should be based on the A.H. molecule.

>close hatch
Okay, the entry hatch is now closed.

>fill tank
The sea water quickly fills the tank, up to the level of the walkway.

>put capsule in reactor
Okay.

>close reactor
Okay, the reactor is now closed.

>turn on reactor
Electrical systems now activated.
(Your score just went up by 5 points!)

>ask tip for tool
Tip hands you the Universal Tool.

>open access panel with tool
Okay, the access panel is now open.

>enter crawl space
(crawl space)
The space is dimly illuminated by small work lights, but you can see machinery everywhere.
BE CAREFUL: Too much wriggling may pose SERIOUS DANGERS!

>fix regulator with tool
Fixed.

>exit crawl space
(SCIMITAR)
Tip is sitting behind you, checking the instruments.

>close access panel
Okay, the access panel is now closed.

>turn on engine
You can immediately hear the powerful thrum of the hydrojet turbine.
(Your score just went up by 5 points!)

>open gate
Opened (by remote control).

>open throttle
Okay, now that the throttle is set, try pushing the joystick to the east.

>e
The SCIMITAR glides smoothly out of the tank onto the surface of Frobton Bay. You're heading east at 1 sea square per turn.
(Your score just went up by 5 points!)
(This might be a good time to use the command: SAVE.)

