The SCIMITAR noses downward, and sea water begins to wash over your forward viewport. You're now diving at a speed of 5 meters per sea square.
The sea water darkens to a deeper green as you descend from the sunlit surface. Engine and propeller noises come over the hydrophone loudspeaker.
Suddenly a loud warning buzzer begins to ring! The depth finder warning light has begun to glow red.

