From here, you can go east or south into the building.

Tip follows you into the southeast deck.

(storage room)
The room is crowded with supplies and equipment. If you want to find something, you'll have to search for it.

Tip follows you into the storage room.

>get bazooka
(Your score just went up by 5 points!)
You are now holding the bazooka.

>n. e
(southeast deck)
The five Aquadome crew members are off to the west.
Commander Bly is off to the west.

Tip follows you into the southeast deck.

(Aquadome office)
The Aquadome office is small but tidy, with a single door leading out and a good view of the ocean through the window.

Tip follows you into the Aquadome office and begins looking out the window.

>wait
(I assume you mean: wait 10 turns.)
Time passes...

Suddenly Commander Bly comes over and repeats, "Jeff, can we discuss a private matter now?" >yes
Zoe closes the door and says:
"There's a traitor here at the Aquadome, Jeff! I discovered the evidence after we talked on the videophone!"
Do you want to keep waiting? >no

>ask about evidence
"I wanted to make sure the Aquadome sonar equipment would warn us if the Snark approached again. I was worried because the blips on the scope looked fuzzy, as if the system was out of alignment. When I inspected it, I found someone had secretly attached this device to it!"
Zoe takes a small "black box" device from her desk drawer.
Tip says quietly, "Jeff, I'd like to talk with you alone."

>open box with tool
Okay, the black box is now open.

>look in box
After a brief study of the circuit, you deduce its purpose: it was designed to change the sonar output so the ultrasonic pulses make a more complex pattern (for example BURPETY BURP B'DURP) instead of just a simple, clear-cut BURP. This would also make fuzzier blips.

>w
As you start to leave, you notice an oddly shaped metallic object lying under Zoe's desk. It must be the special Fram Bolt Wrench!

Suddenly Mick Antrim appears and says, "I'm going to check out your new SCIMITAR, Jeff!" Mick turns and hurries toward the docking tank.

>get wrench
You are now holding the special Fram Bolt Wrench.

>open office door
Okay, the office door is now open.

>wait
(I assume you mean: wait 10 turns.)
Time passes...
Tip says quietly, "Jeff, I'd like to talk with you alone."
Do you want to keep waiting? >no

>w
(southeast deck)
Amy Lowell is off to the west.
Bill Greenup is off to the west.
Marv Siegel is off to the west.
Doc Horvak is off to the west.

Tip follows you into the southeast deck.

Tip says quietly, "Jeff, did Commander Bly mention any troublemakers among the Aquadome crew?" >yes
"Do you suspect Mick Antrim or Doc Horvak or Marv Siegel?" >yes
"Marv maintains the Aquadome sonar equipment," Tip says, "and we'll need it to warn us if the Snark comes back. Didn't Zoe say something is wrong with it?" >yes
"Jeff, do you think someone tampered with it?" >yes
"Does Marv suspect you've discovered signs of tampering?" >yes

>w
(reception area)

Tip follows you into the reception area.
Amy Lowell is here.
Bill Greenup is here.
Marv Siegel is here.
Doc Horvak is here.

>wait
(I assume you mean: wait 10 turns.)
Time passes...

>wait
(I assume you mean: wait 10 turns.)
Time passes...

Suddenly Mick appears and says, "I thought maybe you had a problem on the way here, Jeff, so I wanted to check on it. Everything seems to be okay now."
Tip flashes you a meaningful glance. Mick Antrim's reaction may be all you need to prove he's NOT the traitor. But you'll have to decide for yourself.

Mick Antrim turns away, then stops and says:
"Jeff, there's no Emergency Survival Unit under your seats in the SCIMITAR. I hear you're planning a new type of unit for the Ultramarine Bioceptor. But the standard unit will fit, and we have one in the storage room.
Would you like one installed, just in case? Bill Greenup and Amy Lowell could do it in a few minutes. Shall I tell 'em to?" >yes
"Okay, we'll install it."
(Your score just went up by 5 points!)
Do you want to keep waiting? >no

>give magazine to doc
Doc quickly reads the article, then flashes you an excited glance.
"Jeff, Thorpe's sea creatures evolved from AMINO-HYDROPHASE. If the Snark's his creation, then I know exactly what drug will tranquilize it! Shall I make some up?" >yes
This will take 5 turns.

>wait
(I assume you mean: wait 10 turns.)
Time passes...
Doc Horvak now comes rushing back, holding an aquatic dart gun. "Okay, Jeff, I've made a special 'trank' to use against an A.H.-type organism! It's loaded in the dart gun. What shall I do with it?"
(Your score just went up by 5 points!)
Do you want to keep waiting? >no

>put dart on claw
(Your score just went up by 5 points!)
Doc Horvak promptly mounts the dart gun on an extensor claw.

>s
(docking tank entrance)
Doc Horvak is off to the north.
Mick Antrim is off to the north.
Marv Siegel is off to the north.

Tip follows you into the docking tank entrance.

>put bazooka on claw
"Good idea! That should stop the Snark! It could disable an enemy sub, too! Shall I do it?" >yes
(Your score just went up by 5 points!)
"Are you ready to take off now, Jeff?" Zoe Bly asks anxiously. >no

>ask tip about grid
"If the Snark stays near the sea floor, Jeff, it may churn up silt. Even with our brass search light on, we might have trouble aiming a weapon. Wouldn't it be easier if we could spot its exact position by sonar?" >yes
"Jeff, our sonarscope shows each sea square as 500 meters across. A blip indicates the APPROXIMATE position of an object. That's not good enough to hit the broad side of a barn! Let me install a fine grid on the sonarscope that'll show a blip's position to within 5 meters, okay?" >yes
"Jeff, I checked the storage room and found a fine grid that'll fit our sonarscope. I can install it quickly! I'll have someone install a fine throttle control, too, for tight maneuvering. It has the same 3 settings, but for small sea squares -- 0, 5, 10, or 15 meters per turn."

